      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Las-Vegas-Nevada/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Las Vegas earned the nickname 'Sin City' for its tolerance of adult entertainment, making it a frequent backdrop for films and music videos.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Vegas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city hosts several museums, from the Neon Museum showcasing mid‑century signs to the Mob Museum and the Las Vegas Natural History Museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Vegas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Las Vegas is home to three major pro teams: the NHL's Vegas Golden Knights, the NFL's Raiders, and the WNBA's Aces, all playing in nearby Paradise.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Vegas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Southern Nevada Water Authority is building a $1.4 billion tunnel to bring water from Lake Mead, a controversial $3.2 billion pipeline spans half the state.",
